{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-22 00:38:20 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-22 07:38:20 Indochina Time  \nCoding-Agent: codex  \nSession-ID: 01a0c501-5311-71f0-94e5-033950e0473d\n\nJ2 SIGNED OFF — Dart uses the shared Jing structural reader and the pinned `cbor` 6.5.1 writer, reproduces the frozen corpus, mirrors J1’s limits and refusal policies, and passes the full CLJD lane.\n\nJ3 SIGNED OFF — The three-host conformance gate is sound after the hardening round; no blocking findings remain.\n\n1. E6 Dart column — ADOPT as written. Signed-zero and vector-list collapses are Dart N/A; the other seven rows are live and refused; Dart never raises `host-collapse`; `BigInt.compareTo` normalization and BOM restoration are required shared-code behavior.\n\n2. No-host vector/list case — ADOPT the documented exception. `coll/set-vector-list-collapse` is encode-unobservable on all current hosts because every public set constructor merges the members first. Its decode twin, `mal/collapse-vector-list-set`, runs and refuses `equality-collapse` on all hosts. The case must be reactivated if any host gains a non-merging construction.\n\n3. Conformance gate — ADOPT. The canonical/refusal digests, resource hash pin, documented-skip-derived case sets, independent raw walker with E3/E4 checks, and hardened write-scan provide sufficient cross-host evidence. The orchestrator’s independent `sha256sum` cross-check closes the remaining external-digest concern. Nothing further is required before declaring steps 1–2 complete.\n\n4. Additive boundary — CONFIRMED. J2/J3 touch only the new Jing CBOR implementation and its fixtures/conformance tests. They do not change existing Jing entry points, backends, `dao.space`, transport, `deps.edn`, `bb.edn`, or `pubspec.yaml`. Completion does not authorize step 3, either owner gate, comparator wiring, backend migration, or rebuild cutover.\n\n5. Design-document debt — UNSATISFIED but non